<title>DUBAI: Iran's NIOC says lowers bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Iran's NIOC says lowers bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Iranian Oil Company (NIOC) said on Wednesday it cut 280-cst straight-run fuel oil to $102.50 a tonne from Kharg Island and $97.50 a tonne from Bandar Mahshahr.</p>
<p>The new rates telexed to Reuters by NIOC, took effect on May 28.</p>
<p>Last week's prices stood at $104 a tonne and $99 a tonne from the respective terminals.</p>
<p>Iran bunker fuel is competing against supplies in the United Arab Emirates, Kuwait and Saudi Arabia, traders said.</p>
</text>
